# JavaScript Standards

## Critical Rules

### 1. Use Arrow Function IIFE Pattern
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Arrow function IIFE
(() => {
	// All code here
	// 'use strict' is implicit in modern JS
})();

// ❌ Wrong - Old function-based IIFE
( function() {
	'use strict';
	// Code
} )();
```

### 2. No Inline Event Handlers
```php
// ❌ NEVER do this
<button onclick="handleClick()">Click</button>
<a href="#" onmouseover="doSomething()">Hover</a>

// ✅ Always use addEventListener
<button class="js-button" data-action="submit">Click</button>
```

```javascript
const button = document.querySelector('.js-button');
button.addEventListener('click', handleClick);
```

### 3. Use Tabs for Indentation
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - tabs
(() => {
	const element = document.querySelector('.element');
	if (element) {
		element.classList.add('js-active');
	}
})();
```

## Formatting Rules

### NO Spaces Inside Parentheses
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Standard JS formatting
if (condition) { }
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) { }
while (condition) { }
switch (value) { }

document.querySelector('.selector');
element.addEventListener('click', handler);
functionName(arg1, arg2);

// ❌ Wrong - WordPress PHP style spaces
if ( condition ) { }
document.querySelector( '.selector' );
functionName( arg1, arg2 );
```

### Spaces Around Operators
```javascript
// ✅ Correct
const result = a + b;
const isValid = value === true;
const fullName = firstName + ' ' + lastName;
```

### Array & Object Spacing
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - No spaces inside brackets
const array = [1, 2, 3];
const object = { key: 'value' };

// Multi-line
const config = {
	option1: true,
	option2: 'value',
	option3: [1, 2, 3],
};
```

## Variable Declarations

### Use const and let (Never var)
```javascript
// ✅ Correct
const CONSTANT_VALUE = 'immutable';
const element = document.querySelector('.element');

let counter = 0;
let isActive = false;

// ❌ Wrong - Never use var
var element = document.querySelector('.element');
var counter = 0;
```

### Const by Default
```javascript
// ✅ Use const unless you need to reassign
const items = [];
items.push('item'); // ✅ OK - mutating array, not reassigning

let counter = 0;
counter++; // ✅ OK - reassigning value

// ❌ Wrong - Using let when const would work
let element = document.querySelector('.element');
// element is never reassigned
```

## Naming Conventions

### camelCase for Variables and Functions
```javascript
// ✅ Correct
const headerNavToggle = document.querySelector('.header-nav-toggle');
const handleClick = (event) => { };
let isMenuOpen = false;

// CSS classes use 'js-' prefix
const activeClass = 'js-active';
const popupActiveClass = 'js-popup-active';

// ❌ Wrong
const header_nav_toggle = document.querySelector('.header-nav-toggle');
const HandleClick = (event) => { };
```

## Functions

### Arrow Functions (Preferred)
```javascript
// ✅ Preferred - Arrow functions
const handleClick = (event) => {
	event.preventDefault();
	// Handle click
};

const formatPrice = (price) => `$${price.toFixed(2)}`;

const sum = (a, b) => a + b;

// Arrow functions in callbacks
elements.forEach((element) => {
	element.classList.add('js-active');
});
```

### Early Returns
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Early returns for cleaner code
const processData = (data) => {
	if (!data) return null;
	if (!data.items) return null;
	if (data.items.length === 0) return [];

	return data.items.map(processItem);
};

// ❌ Wrong - Nested conditionals
const processData = (data) => {
	if (data) {
		if (data.items) {
			if (data.items.length > 0) {
				return data.items.map(processItem);
			}
		}
	}
	return null;
};
```

## DOM Manipulation

### Selecting Elements
```javascript
// ✅ Correct
const element = document.querySelector('.selector');
const elements = document.querySelectorAll('.selector');
const byId = document.getElementById('element-id');

// With early return for null check
const element = document.querySelector('.selector');
if (!element) return;
```

### Creating Elements
```javascript
const createCard = (data) => {
	const card = document.createElement('article');
	card.className = 'card';
	card.innerHTML = `
		<h2 class="card__title">${escapeHtml(data.title)}</h2>
		<p class="card__content">${escapeHtml(data.content)}</p>
	`;
	return card;
};
```

### Event Handling
```javascript
// ✅ Named handler function
const handleSubmit = (event) => {
	event.preventDefault();
	const form = event.currentTarget;
	const data = new FormData(form);
	// Process form
};

form.addEventListener('submit', handleSubmit);

// Arrow function in listener
headerNavToggle.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
	e.preventDefault();
	toggleNavigation();
});
```

## DOM Ready Patterns

### Standard Pattern
```javascript
(() => {
	// Cache elements
	const element = document.querySelector('.element');

	// Early return if element doesn't exist
	if (!element) return;

	// Initialize functionality
	const init = () => {
		setupEventListeners();
		// Other initialization
	};

	const setupEventListeners = () => {
		element.addEventListener('click', handleClick);
	};

	init();
})();
```

### Multiple Initializations
```javascript
(() => {
	const initNavigation = () => {
		const nav = document.querySelector('.header-nav');
		if (!nav) return;
		// Setup navigation
	};

	const initSliders = () => {
		const sliders = document.querySelectorAll('.swiper');
		if (!sliders.length) return;
		// Setup sliders
	};

	initNavigation();
	initSliders();
})();
```

## Async Operations

### Async/Await (Preferred)
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - async/await
const fetchData = async (url) => {
	try {
		const response = await fetch(url);

		if (!response.ok) {
			throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
		}

		return await response.json();
	} catch (error) {
		console.error('Fetch error:', error);
		return null;
	}
};
```

### WordPress AJAX
```javascript
const submitForm = async (formData) => {
	try {
		const response = await fetch(localizeVar.adminUrl, {
			method: 'POST',
			credentials: 'same-origin',
			body: new URLSearchParams({
				action: 'skel_submit_form',
				nonce: localizeVar.nonce,
				...Object.fromEntries(formData),
			}),
		});

		const data = await response.json();

		if (!data.success) {
			throw new Error(data.data.message || 'Unknown error');
		}

		return data.data;
	} catch (error) {
		console.error('AJAX error:', error);
		throw error;
	}
};
```

## Class Toggling Patterns

### Standard Toggle
```javascript
const activeClass = 'js-active';

// Add class
element.classList.add(activeClass);

// Remove class
element.classList.remove(activeClass);

// Toggle class
element.classList.toggle(activeClass);

// Check class
if (element.classList.contains(activeClass)) {
	// Do something
}
```

### Toggle with ARIA
```javascript
const openNavigation = () => {
	headerNavToggle.classList.add(activeClass);
	headerNav.classList.add(activeClass);
	body.classList.add(popupActiveClass);

	// Update ARIA attributes
	headerNavToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
	headerNav.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
};

const closeNavigation = () => {
	headerNavToggle.classList.remove(activeClass);
	headerNav.classList.remove(activeClass);
	body.classList.remove(popupActiveClass);

	// Update ARIA attributes
	headerNavToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
	headerNav.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
};
```

## Data Attributes

### Reading Data Attributes
```javascript
const toggleClick = element.getAttribute('data-toggle-click');
const toggleGroup = element.getAttribute('data-toggle-group');

// Check if attribute exists
if (element.hasAttribute('data-tab')) {
	// Do something
}
```

### Setting Data Attributes
```javascript
element.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
element.setAttribute('data-inview', 'true');

// Remove attribute
element.removeAttribute('data-lenis-prevent');
```

## Event Delegation
```javascript
// Event delegation pattern
document.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
	const button = event.target.closest('.js-button');
	if (!button) return;

	handleButtonClick(button);
});
```

## Error Handling

### Try/Catch Pattern
```javascript
const safeJsonParse = (jsonString) => {
	try {
		return JSON.parse(jsonString);
	} catch (error) {
		console.error('JSON parse error:', error);
		return null;
	}
};
```

## Common Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Never Do This
```javascript
// Global variables
myGlobalVar = 'bad';

// Using var
var element = document.querySelector('.element');

// Inline handlers in HTML
<button onclick="doSomething()">

// Spaces in control structures (this is PHP style, not JS)
if ( condition ) { }
document.querySelector( '.selector' );

// Not handling errors
fetch(url).then(r => r.json()).then(data => console.log(data));

// Using eval
eval('code');
```

### ✅ Do This Instead
```javascript
// Arrow function IIFE
(() => {
	const localVar = 'good';

	// Use const/let
	const element = document.querySelector('.element');

	// Event listeners
	element.addEventListener('click', handleClick);

	// Standard spacing
	if (condition) {
		doSomething();
	}

	// Error handling
	try {
		const data = await fetch(url).then(r => r.json());
		console.log(data);
	} catch (error) {
		console.error(error);
	}
})();
```

## Accessibility Considerations

```javascript
// Focus management
const openModal = (modal) => {
	modal.hidden = false;
	modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');

	// Focus first focusable element
	const firstFocusable = modal.querySelector(
		'button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])'
	);
	firstFocusable?.focus();
};

// Keyboard navigation
const handleKeydown = (event) => {
	switch (event.key) {
		case 'ArrowDown':
			event.preventDefault();
			focusNextItem();
			break;
		case 'ArrowUp':
			event.preventDefault();
			focusPreviousItem();
			break;
		case 'Escape':
			closeMenu();
			break;
	}
};
```
